End-to-End Dashboard & Impact
I designed, deployed, and managed a centralized Tableau dashboard connecting directly to Snowflake views to operationalize these insights.

Design & Wireframing: Built top-level executive summary KPIs (Global Active Learners, Course Completion Rate, Avg. Time-to-Completion) backed by granular filters for subscription tiers and regional cohorts.

Adoption & Access Control: Published to Tableau Server with role-based permissions (CSMs only viewed their assigned enterprise accounts).

Business Impact:

Weekly active dashboard users grew by 65% within the first month.

The analysis uncovered a 40% drop-off rate in a specific technical onboarding module.

Partnering with the Product and UX teams to streamline this bottleneck improved overall cohort completion rates by 18% the following quarter.

📈 Key Learnings & Takeaways
Performance Tuning Matters: Moving away from querying raw, unindexed event logs down to partitioned, pre-aggregated tables cut core reporting query times from minutes to under 5 seconds.

Data Must Be Actionable: Partnering closely with stakeholders ensured that the anomaly-detection model didn't just report numbers, but actively triggered automated CSM workflows before renewal dates.
